Stage 3 Lab Activities – SmartCare Domain Modelling
AI off - AI on - compare - Verify
A — Requirements Review (SmartCare v0.2)
Nouns (candidate concepts)
- Patient
- Practitioner
- Appointment
- Schedule
- Availability
- Record
- Status
- Report
- Booking
- History

Verbs (behaviours / operations)
- Create patient records
- Search patient records
- Book appointments
- Cancel appointments
- Update status
- View schedule
- Generate reports

Business Rules
- No double-booking allowed
- Appointment must link a patient and practitioner
- Appointment status must be tracked
- Patient and practitioner records must be searchable
- System must maintain appointment history

B- Candidate Class:
| Concept       | Class? | Supporting Requirements                | State/Behaviour                         |
|---------------|--------|----------------------------------------|------------------------------------------|
| Patient       | Yes    | FR-01, FR-02, FR-10                    | name, contact, history                   |
| Practitioner  | Yes    | FR-03, FR-04, FR-09                    | name, availability, schedule             |
| Appointment   | Yes    | FR-05, FR-06, FR-07, FR-08, FR-10      | date, time, status, patient, practitioner|
| Status        | No     | FR-08                                  | attribute of Appointment                 |
| Cancellation  | No     | FR-07                                  | event, not a class                       |
| Report        | No     | FR-11                                  | output, not a class                      |
| Clinic        | Maybe  | Optional aggregation                    | system-level container                   |
| Database      | No     | NFR-03                                 | implementation detail                    |

